{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44129756",
      "title": "Reactive Forms: Getting Started",
      "lectureOrder": 251,
      "videoOrder": 239,
      "sourceHash": "c34bcea3313af43924e795cbe4b1aeecab95ec6b8b44dff297774fef72af5daa",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.04,
          "en": "So, now that we learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 5.73,
          "en": "about this template-driven forms approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.73,
          "end": 8.88,
          "en": "we'll move on to the reactive forms approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.88,
          "end": 12.48,
          "en": "which is that other main way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.48,
          "end": 14.943,
          "en": "of handling forms Angular gives you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.2,
          "end": 20.64,
          "en": "Now, for that, I completely reset my login component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.64,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "and you find the updated login component HTML",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "and TypeScript files attached to therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.81,
          "end": 30.54,
          "en": "so that you can reset yours as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.54,
          "end": 33.45,
          "en": "because we will now handle this form again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.45,
          "end": 36.81,
          "en": "but now using this reactive forms approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.81,
          "end": 39.15,
          "en": "And, of course, later we will also move on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.15,
          "end": 42.33,
          "en": "to the signup form which is a bit more complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.33,
          "end": 45.69,
          "en": "because it's a longer form with more input elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.69,
          "end": 49.503,
          "en": "But for the basics, we'll start with this login component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.43,
          "end": 53.01,
          "en": "So, how do we now register",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.01,
          "end": 57.39,
          "en": "and handle this form with the reactive forms approach?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 60.93,
          "en": "Well, one important difference is that unlike",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.93,
          "end": 63.66,
          "en": "with the template-driven approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.66,
          "end": 67.893,
          "en": "we don't set up the form in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.78999999999999,
          "end": 73.78999999999999,
          "en": "We will later connect the template elements to our form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.37,
          "end": 76.92,
          "en": "but we don't register them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.92,
          "end": 80.67,
          "en": "We don't initialize the form with help of the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.67,
          "end": 83.973,
          "en": "Instead, we do that in our TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.87,
          "end": 86.67,
          "en": "And to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.67,
          "end": 90.66,
          "en": "we simply go to our component that holds our form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.66,
          "end": 93.33,
          "en": "so to the login component in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.33,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "and there you can simply add a new property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 103.07,
          "en": "called form or myForm, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.65,
          "end": 106.2,
          "en": "The name does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.2,
          "end": 110.52000000000001,
          "en": "The value of this property does matter though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.52000000000001,
          "end": 114.60300000000001,
          "en": "because that should be an object of type FormGroup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 116.38900000000001,
          "end": 119.67,
          "en": "and that is something that's imported from Angular forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 119.67,
          "end": 122.58,
          "en": "and that is actually a class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.58,
          "end": 126,
          "en": "And therefore, you should instantiate a new instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 126,
          "end": 128.61,
          "en": "of this FormGroup class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.61,
          "end": 131.79,
          "en": "because a form in Angular is, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "a FormGroup object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 135.48,
          "en": "And you saw that before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.48,
          "end": 139.5,
          "en": "with the template-driven forms approach as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 142.74,
          "en": "When we logged that form there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 142.74,
          "end": 144.03,
          "en": "you saw that in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.03,
          "end": 147.21,
          "en": "it was an object of TypeForm group.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.21,
          "end": 149.94,
          "en": "Now with the reactive forms approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.94,
          "end": 154.8,
          "en": "we create this FormGroup object on our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.8,
          "end": 158.73,
          "en": "Now, such a FormGroup takes an object as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 158.73,
          "end": 159.78,
          "en": "as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.78,
          "end": 161.1,
          "en": "and it's that object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.1,
          "end": 165.45,
          "en": "that now registers multiple key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.45,
          "end": 170.45,
          "en": "where every key value pair represents one control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.99,
          "end": 176.99,
          "en": "inside of that FormGroup or some nested FormGroup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.3,
          "end": 180.9,
          "en": "And I'll get back to nested FormGroups later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.9,
          "end": 184.53,
          "en": "For the moment, let's focus on individual controls.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.53,
          "end": 188.46,
          "en": "So if I wanna register an email control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 191.34,
          "en": "for my email input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 191.34,
          "end": 194.58,
          "en": "I could do that by adding a key named email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 194.58,
          "end": 197.25,
          "en": "Though that name also doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 197.25,
          "end": 199.23,
          "en": "It's totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.23,
          "end": 202.633,
          "en": "But the type now must be a new FormControl.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204,
          "end": 207.48,
          "en": "So for that, we import FormControl from Angular forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.48,
          "end": 210.03,
          "en": "and instantiate that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.03,
          "end": 213.27,
          "en": "Now the FormControl constructor can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 215.43,
          "en": "without any arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 215.43,
          "end": 218.82,
          "en": "to set up a FormControl without any initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 218.82,
          "end": 220.95,
          "en": "or any other information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 220.95,
          "end": 224.64,
          "en": "But you can, for example, also pass one argument to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 224.64,
          "end": 228.09,
          "en": "to give that FormControl an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 228.09,
          "end": 233.09,
          "en": "For example, here to give it an initial empty value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 233.73,
          "end": 237.12,
          "en": "And of course, we can now also add a second input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 237.12,
          "end": 240.18,
          "en": "a second control, the password FormControl,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 240.18,
          "end": 243.15,
          "en": "which also has an empty initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.15,
          "end": 243.983,
          "en": "And with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 243.983,
          "end": 247.65,
          "en": "we created a form with the reactive forms approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 247.65,
          "end": 250.5,
          "en": "and we could now use that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 250.5,
          "end": 253.47,
          "en": "For example, I could add onSubmit method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 253.47,
          "end": 255.96,
          "en": "which currently is never triggered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.96,
          "end": 257.7,
          "en": "but we'll take care of that soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.7,
          "end": 258.63,
          "en": "But I could add it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.63,
          "end": 262.47,
          "en": "and in there, I could reach out to my form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.47,
          "end": 265.23,
          "en": "and for example, access the form value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 265.23,
          "end": 269.73,
          "en": "and then access the email control value here and use that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 269.73,
          "end": 271.26,
          "en": "Though of course at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 271.26,
          "end": 274.2,
          "en": "that would always be that empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.2,
          "end": 279.2,
          "en": "since at the moment we have a form with which we could work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.57,
          "end": 283.23,
          "en": "but which is not connected to our template form here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.23,
          "end": 285.9,
          "en": "to our markup at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 285.9,
          "end": 290.64,
          "en": "And that's therefore the next important setup step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 290.64,
          "end": 295.11,
          "en": "you need to go through when working with reactive forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 295.11,
          "end": 299.43,
          "en": "The first step is that you set up the form on your own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 299.43,
          "end": 301.5,
          "en": "in your TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 301.5,
          "end": 304.47,
          "en": "But the second step then is that you still need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 304.47,
          "end": 309.03,
          "en": "to let Angular know how this form is connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 309.03,
          "end": 310.89,
          "en": "to your actual template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 310.89,
          "end": 314.73,
          "en": "to your actual input elements in your markup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 314.73,
          "end": 316.713,
          "en": "And that's what we'll do next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
